{
  "about": "Fixed test vectors for the zkb.fi fee rules (explorer/shared/src/fee-rules.ts). Every number is an integer written as a decimal string: token amounts in base units, gas prices in wei, money in USD scaled by 1e18 like wei (1 USD = 1000000000000000000), shares of the amount scaled by 1e18 (1% = 10000000000000000), prices as USD per whole token scaled by 1e18. null means 'no price'. Each list holds { input, output } pairs for the function of the same name; an SDK must give exactly these outputs.",
  "rounding": "One rule: every division rounds down (truncates), toward the user. Thresholds are compared exactly by cross-multiplying, never rounded. The default curve's power is computed as 1% x exp(-ln(amount/10) x ln10/ln50) in 1e36 fixed point (ln by halving plus the atanh series, exp by ln2 range reduction plus the Taylor series, each term truncated, stopping at the first zero term), then truncated to 1e18.",
